Goal: author H15 PATCH validation tests without editing implementation

memory:
  task_brief
  route_policy
  policy_version

flow:
  remember key="policy_version" value="h15-patch-test-authoring-local-screen-v1"
  remember key="route_policy" value="Local worker owns src/test.js only. src/app.js already contains the implementation and must not be edited. Hidden oracle details are not available."

  prompt: Read TASK.md, src/app.js, and src/test.js. Add executable PATCH validation tests in src/test.js only. Preserve the existing test(name, fn) helper and existing listContacts, getContact, createContact, deleteContact, and patchContact test(...) blocks. Do not replace them with a different harness. Do not edit src/app.js. The app functions return response objects with status and body fields; do not treat them as raw contacts and do not expect validation failures to throw. Add at least eight PATCH validation tests covering invalid short name, invalid long name, invalid email without a dot after @, invalid email without @, invalid phone characters, invalid short phone, empty company string, null company accepted, partial update preservation, and missing ID behavior. Use fresh contacts created with createContact for PATCH tests when test order could mutate shared contact state. For partial update preservation, create a fresh contact and copy primitive expected values into separate variables such as originalEmail, originalPhone, and originalCompany before calling patchContact; do not compare against a live getContact(...).body object reference after mutation. Include literal edge inputs for email: 'bad@domain', email: 'bad.domain', phone: '123456', company: '', company: null, and patchContact(999, ...). Run node src/test.js. When the tests pass, respond with a concise status that names src/test.js as the only changed file so the flow can continue.

  retry max 4
    run: node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const tests=fs.readFileSync('src/test.js','utf8'); const app=fs.readFileSync('src/app.js','utf8'); const validationTests=(tests.match(/test\\s*\\(\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*(patch|validation|invalid|reject|short|long|email|phone|company|null|partial|missing)[^'\\\"]*['\\\"]/gi)||[]).length; const patchCalls=(tests.match(/patchContact\\s*\\(/g)||[]).length; const required=[[/name:\\s*['\\\"]A['\\\"]/,'short name'],[/repeat\\(101\\)/,'long name'],[/email:\\s*['\\\"]bad@domain['\\\"]|email:\\s*['\\\"]test@domain['\\\"]/,'email without dot after @'],[/email:\\s*['\\\"]bad\\.domain['\\\"]|email:\\s*['\\\"]testdomain\\.com['\\\"]/,'email without @'],[/phone:\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*[A-Za-z!][^'\\\"]*['\\\"]/,'invalid phone characters'],[/phone:\\s*['\\\"]123456['\\\"]/,'short phone'],[/company:\\s*['\\\"]{2}/,'empty company string'],[/company:\\s*null/,'null company'],[/patchContact\\(\\s*999/,'missing ID']]; if (!/require\\(['\\\"]\\.\\/app['\\\"]\\)/.test(tests) || !tests.includes('patchContact')) { console.error('patchContact import missing'); process.exit(1); } if (validationTests < 8 || patchCalls < 9) { console.error('expected at least 8 validation tests and 9 patchContact calls, found tests='+validationTests+' calls='+patchCalls); process.exit(1); } const missing=required.filter(([pattern])=>!pattern.test(tests)).map(([,label])=>label); if (missing.length) { console.error('missing required PATCH validation cases: '+missing.join(', ')); process.exit(1); } for (const original of ['listContacts returns all','getContact returns existing','createContact succeeds','deleteContact preserves 204 null success behavior','patchContact valid name update works']) { if (!tests.includes(original)) { console.error('existing test removed: '+original); process.exit(1); } } if (!app.includes('function hasValidEmailShape') || !app.includes('function hasValidPhoneShape')) { console.error('src/app.js appears changed or incomplete'); process.exit(1); }"
    if command_failed
      prompt: The H15 test-authoring structural gate failed. Fix src/test.js only. Keep the existing test(name, fn) helper and original test(...) blocks; app functions return { status, body } response objects and validation failures return 400 responses instead of throwing. Import and call patchContact, preserve existing tests, and add executable PATCH validation tests covering every requested case: short name, long name, email without dot after @, email without @, invalid phone characters, short phone, empty company string, null company accepted, partial update preservation, and missing ID. Prefer fresh createContact records for PATCH tests so one test does not mutate data required by a later test. For partial update preservation, snapshot primitive expected values before calling patchContact; do not compare against a live object returned by getContact after patchContact mutates it. Do not edit src/app.js. After the fix, finish with a done action and a concise status. Gate output: ${last_stdout} ${last_stderr}
    end
  end

  retry max 6
    run: node src/test.js [timeout 120]
    if command_failed
      prompt: Public tests are failing. Fix src/test.js only so the existing implementation passes and the PATCH validation tests are executable. Keep the existing test(name, fn) helper and use result.status/result.body response objects. For partial update preservation, snapshot primitive expected field values before calling patchContact. Do not edit src/app.js. After the fix, finish with a done action and a concise status. Test output: ${last_stdout} ${last_stderr}
    end
  end

  prompt: Use a write_file action to create local-worker-summary.md at the workspace root. Include changed files, checks run, failures, timeout/no-edit status, inputArtifactRefs, outputArtifactRefs, and diffSummary. Do not mention or infer hidden oracle implementation details.

  retry max 2
    run: node -e "process.exit(require('node:fs').existsSync('local-worker-summary.md') ? 0 : 1)"
    if command_failed
      prompt: local-worker-summary.md is still missing. Use a write_file action now to create local-worker-summary.md at the workspace root with changed files, checks run, failures, timeout/no-edit status, inputArtifactRefs, outputArtifactRefs, and diffSummary.
    end
  end

done when:
  file_exists local-worker-summary.md
  gate tests_authored: node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const tests=fs.readFileSync('src/test.js','utf8'); const app=fs.readFileSync('src/app.js','utf8'); const validationTests=(tests.match(/test\\s*\\(\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*(patch|validation|invalid|reject|short|long|email|phone|company|null|partial|missing)[^'\\\"]*['\\\"]/gi)||[]).length; const patchCalls=(tests.match(/patchContact\\s*\\(/g)||[]).length; const required=[/name:\\s*['\\\"]A['\\\"]/, /repeat\\(101\\)/, /email:\\s*['\\\"]bad@domain['\\\"]|email:\\s*['\\\"]test@domain['\\\"]/, /email:\\s*['\\\"]bad\\.domain['\\\"]|email:\\s*['\\\"]testdomain\\.com['\\\"]/, /phone:\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*[A-Za-z!][^'\\\"]*['\\\"]/, /phone:\\s*['\\\"]123456['\\\"]/, /company:\\s*['\\\"]{2}/, /company:\\s*null/, /patchContact\\(\\s*999/]; if (validationTests<8||patchCalls<9) process.exit(1); if (required.some((pattern)=>!pattern.test(tests))) process.exit(1); if (!app.includes('function hasValidEmailShape')||!app.includes('function hasValidPhoneShape')) process.exit(1);"
  gate public_tests: node src/test.js
